# tp4/next-2 window: this is tp4-w2-kill-jobs/K-W2b-kill-switch re-pointed at the integrated image tp4-next2-1 (B0 of this pack, built from the tp4/next-2 head = tp4/octo-2 + tp4/prod-fixes); where the text below
# says tp4/prod-fixes or the window branch read tp4/next-2, and the image tag placeholder is tp4-next2-1 (sed -i 's/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/' *.env). ORDER.txt of this pack has the order and the minutes.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the W2 kill-switch drill (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prod-fixes (or of
# a branch that carries it) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from
# this branch by its author. ONE IMAGE FOR THE DRILL: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head (sed -i "s/tp4-next2-1/<tag>/" *.env). A commit of a file the
# image carries (w2_switch.py is one) needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. The cards are under development: this drill never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# K-W2b (STOP): the W2 KILL SWITCH drill on the production stack (Lever N + prefix reuse + W2 + engine reuse, unaudited): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-kill is the ship profile plus the gate-only
# drill QWEN_FAST_W2_OFF_AFTER=480 with QWEN_FAST_W2_OFF_PATH=/tmp/qwen-w2.off (docs/tp4-w2-kill-switch.md): after 480 packed rounds (both blocks together) the SERVER writes the flag file inside the container and the ordinary
# poll latches the switch, so nobody touches a file mid-job (K1 of the engine-reuse pack latches parked.off the same way) and the real file path is the one exercised. The traffic, in order: concurrent8_steady (eight users,
# 800 tokens each: W2 packed rounds, about 320 block rounds), concurrent8_code_equal (eight users, 800 tokens each: the kill lands about half way through it, the rest of its rounds are the sequential step's), one coding answer.
# Knowingly the eight-seat rules of c2_smoke_check judge the steady test on the rounds BEFORE the latch only; read them against the log.
# READ (c2_smoke_check, whose w2_kill_problems requires all of it when the profile sets the trigger): exactly one '[PINDIAG] w2 kill switch drill (gate only): wrote /tmp/qwen-w2.off after 480 packed rounds' line, then
# exactly one '[PINDIAG] w2 kill switch /tmp/qwen-w2.off present: packed rounds ...' latch line, at least one '[PINDIAG] packed extent round' line BEFORE it and NONE after it (every packed round replays a trace that carries
# W2: the markers stop), a '[PINDIAG] w2 kill switch routed the round to the sequential step' line after it, no 'present at attach' line, every request completes (no stall, no crash, no abort), the tp4 sdpa engaged
# line (config=multi flags=0x21) and the conv-gates spread engaged line BEFORE the latch. THEN offline: python3 scripts/ci/levern_compare.py --control <K-W2a smoke log> --levern <K-W2b smoke log> (exit 0: every
# stream's content hash, reasoning hash, token count and finish reason of every test equal to K-W2a's - the text the kill arm served, packed before the latch and sequential after it, is the W2-off control's text).
# NO-GO for the kill switch: a latch line without the drill line, packed rounds after the latch, a hash difference, a stall, a request that did not complete, the sequential rounds slower than 10 s a round (record the
# per-round time after the latch: the brown-out must be bounded). Duration (estimate): 70 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-next2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-kill
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_equal,coding
C2_BOX_MINUTES=90
